    "Potential recipients of antitachyarrhythmia devices should undergo extensive testing before implantation to ensure the devices safely and reliably terminate tachyarrhythmias without causing proarrhythmia. Permanent pacing can be used in certain conditions, including symptomatic recurrent SVT, sustained pause-dependent VT, and congenital long-QT syndrome. There is evidence supporting pacing for preventing atrial fibrhythmias in selected scenarios. The efficacy of atrial overdrive pacing in atrial fibrillation is still being studied.": {
      "Long-QT Syndrome is associated with the use of cardiac pacing with beta-blockade for symptom prevention in congenital conditions, potentially addressing pause-dependent tachyarrhythmias or bradycardia associated with it. While primary benefits may be observed, long-term survival improvement remains undetermined.": []
